From 82602c7fbdcda5ef2eab44a21e5c6a9cd4f7d7f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:28:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/69] Input: nt36xxx-spi: Port to mainline and add NT36672C
 support

Changes on top of the imported vendor driver:

- Port to current APIs: GPIO descriptors instead of of_gpio, the IRQ from
  the devicetree "interrupts" property; drop the Xiaomi display notifier
  and the MediaTek-only SPI setup.
- Detect the chip instead of hardcoding the NT36523 memory map
  (nvt_ts_check_chip_ver_trim from Motorola's nova_0flash_mmi driver).
  NT36672C uses the NT36675 map, identical in both drivers.
- Find the firmware image size from the "NVT"/"MOD" end flag, and use
  Motorola's binary header parser and HW CRC download order; with the
  NT36523 sequence the download completed but the firmware never started.
- Abort the probe cleanly if the firmware download fails (previously the
  probe continued with ts->mmap NULL and crashed).
- Take the fallback touch area from touchscreen-size-x/y.
- Mark the ESD check workqueue WQ_UNBOUND.

The NT36672C-specific code paths are taken from Motorola's GPL
nova_0flash_mmi driver (android_kernel_motorola_sm7250).

Tested on nairo with linux-next 20261002 plus the SM7250 v9 series ("Add
support for SM7250", patches 03/04/09/10/11/12). The firmware
(novatek_ts_fw.bin from the LineageOS vendor partition) downloads in
about 90 ms, the chip reports fw_ver 0x05 / PID 601D, and evtest shows
correct coordinates in all four corners. This driver is a bring-up
vehicle, not in a state suitable for upstream as is.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

